module gunbc.explicit_witness_admission

import std.realization_schedule {
  ScheduleWitnessEntry,
  WitnessKind,
  CorpusWitnessKind,
  ExecutionWitnessKind,
  witness_kind_eq
}
import std.witness_admission {
  WitnessConsumerCadence,
  DiscoverySelection,
  FalsifierSelfHostWet,
  FalsifierRehomedBinWet,
  FalsifierSubstrateLongLane,
  BinWitnessWet,
  QuarantineProbeExpectRed,
  OfflineLocalRecipe,
  FixtureExplicitRoster,
  NoConsumer
}
import std.types { NonEmptyStr, String, List, Bool, Int }

data explicit_witness_admission_authority_note: String = "THE function-grain authority for exact witness admission. One row per admitted witness, carrying the witness identity, the cadence that executes it, and its own reason and dissolve_on. Everything else about that witness is DERIVED: the cadence roster the scheduler runs, the discovery exclusion, and the consumer manifest all read these rows; none of them is authored beside them. It replaces a DUAL REPRESENTATION carried until 2026-08-03 — a path-substring WitnessExclusionRow classified QuarantineProbeExpectRed (removing a whole FILE from discovery) sitting beside a probe_red(entry, f) roster row (enrolling one FUNCTION on the probe cadence). Those are not the same fact, but they were two hand-kept representations of one admission relationship with nothing deriving either from the other, and the reconciliation that guarded them was weaker than its name: it proved only that some scheduled row's entry CONTAINED the exclusion pattern as a substring. It proved neither exact identity, nor one schedule row per exclusion, nor reverse coverage, nor that every function hidden by the file-level exclusion had a consumer, nor that the pair deleted atomically. The cost was paid in a real merge: #7688 had to delete one exclusion/probe pair while hand-preserving two newly added ones, and taking either side wholesale would have dropped required admission rows with no conflict marker. The exact grain also dissolves the trade that forced the workaround: a green sibling in a quarantined file used to be excluded with it, so an author had to split the file or downgrade its classification and say so in prose (the receipt is the self_host_03_normalize exclusion row, whose reason reads that QuarantineProbeExpectRed on the file would orphan its sibling). A row here reaches exactly one function; siblings are untouched."

data explicit_witness_admission_separation_note: String = "SEPARATION FROM PATH POLICY (operator ruling, this lane). Exact witness admission and broad path policy are different kinds of fact and must not share a substring-based representation — that fusion is the root of the substring-overlap weakness above. Directory- and file-wide policies (`test/claim/long/` is the long-test home; `test/manual/` is offline) stay in gunbc.ci_layer_roots witness_exclusion_frontier, which is now a PATH POLICY carrier only: witness_exclusion_row_well_formed REFUSES a QuarantineProbeExpectRed row there, so the fused representation is unwritable for this cadence rather than merely reconciled. PRECEDENCE, and it is total: a function with an exact admission is decided by that admission; path policy applies only to functions with none. That is why a path-offline file may legitimately contain an exact-admitted function (self_host_03_normalize_behavioral_witness_test.dag: the receipt is quarantined here, its sibling is offline by the file's path row) without either fact restating the other. THE REMAINING FUSION IS COUNTED, NOT SILENT: BinWitnessWet, FalsifierRehomedBinWet, FalsifierSubstrateLongLane and FalsifierSelfHostWet still author a path row beside their function-grain rosters. Their populations are not the bad state today — every one is either a file-grain roster row (ScheduleWitnessEntry's empty-function form, which covers every function in the entry by construction) or fully enumerated, measured on this change's tree — so they are a migration frontier, not a live defect. Dissolve-on: each cadence's roster moves into explicit_witness_admissions and its path rows delete, at which point witness_exclusion_row_well_formed refuses that cadence too and the last enum arm that can appear in the path carrier is gone."

type ExplicitWitnessAdmission {
  witness: ScheduleWitnessEntry
  cadence: WitnessConsumerCadence
  reason: NonEmptyStr
  dissolve_on: NonEmptyStr
}

fn known_red_probe(
  entry: NonEmptyStr,
  f: String,
  kind: WitnessKind,
  reason: NonEmptyStr,
  dissolve_on: NonEmptyStr
) -> ExplicitWitnessAdmission {
  ExplicitWitnessAdmission {
    witness: ScheduleWitnessEntry { entry: entry, function: f, kind: kind },
    cadence: QuarantineProbeExpectRed,
    reason: reason,
    dissolve_on: dissolve_on
  }
}

data known_red_class_note: String = "WHAT A KNOWN-RED ADMISSION IS: a witness red on main for a feature gap owned by a named lane. It is a RED CONTROL for that lane, not a broken test — deleting it would discard the discriminating input, while leaving it in per-PR discovery would red every wide PR on a debt that PR did not create. Greening is the counted un-quarantine event of std.witness_admission: the row deletes in the SAME change that lands the fix, which promotes the unchanged witness to ordinary DiscoverySelection as a permanent regression control (DESIGN 4b(4) — the climb deletes the quarantine machinery, never the evidence). The roster must not grow silently: a new admission carries a reason naming the diagnosis and owner plus a dissolve_on, both refused empty by NonEmptyStr, and a row whose witness runs green locally is stale and deletes. Local recipe per row: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <entry> --functions <function>. CorpusWitnessKind rows run on the hermetic falsifier probe batch; ExecutionWitnessKind rows run on the falsifier wet quarantine batch."

